     "flex": 0.295,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "html": "<p>ProblemThe conventional workflow working with prismatic structure is labor-intensive and time-consuming: Noticing the low efficiency, I realized there is a strong need for a digital parametric tool that could be used to accelerate the design iteration process. <br>The tool should enable designers to design and simulate movement in the digital environment to freely (and more efficiently) explore more potential opportunities.</p>",
       "kind": "text"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "flex": 0.705,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "image",
       "src": "transform/05.jpg",
       "width": 1920,
       "height": 1080,
       "kind": "white"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "kind": "row"
  },
  {
   "type": "row",
   "columns": [
    {
     "flex": 0.625,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "image",
       "src": "transform/06.jpg",
       "width": 1442,
       "height": 740,
       "kind": "photo"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "flex": 0.375,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "html": "<h3>Solution</h3>\n<p>Since the goal of this tool is to help people design, it has to be user-friendly and intuitive to use. I decided to use a modular component to represent each unit. This software architecture allows users directly see the connection between individual input parameters and output geometry.</p>",
       "kind": "text"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "kind": "row"
  },
  {
   "type": "row",
   "columns": [
