   "kind": "row"
  },
  {
   "type": "row",
   "columns": [
    {
     "flex": 0.375,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "html": "<h3>Challenge</h3>\n<p>The challenge is to understand the math behind the transformation: The input angle and output angle do not map linearly. At the first attempt, I called intersect functions from RhinoCommon as a hard way to solve the geometrical equation. It works, but the intersection method is a bit clumsy computation-wise.</p>\n<p>I further broke down the geometry relationships into trigonometric equations. This change not only simplify the code and also increase computational efficiency.</p>",
       "kind": "text"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
